==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|diphthérie}}, coined 1857 by {{w|lang=en|Pierre Bretonneau}}; from {{der|en|grc|διφθέρα||prepared hide, leather}}, for the tough membrane that forms in the throat. Bretonneau earlier used {{m|fr|diphthérite}}, from which {{m|en|diphtheritis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/dɪfˈθɪəɹɪə/|/dɪpˈθɪəɹɪə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/dɪfˈθɪɹi.ə/|/dɪpˈθɪɹi.ə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪəɹiə}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪɹiə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A serious [[infectious]] disease which causes inflammation of mucous membranes of the upper [[respiratory tract]] caused by {{taxlink|Corynebacterium diphtheriae|species|noshow=1}}.

